{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/422881-capturing-the-feeling-of-myths","id":422881,"title":"Capturing the feeling of myths","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Onyx Path Worlds","Scion"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-02-28T07:15:04-08:00","id":422881,"title":"Capturing the feeling of myths","content":"<br /> I love mythologies, but my players are pretty ambivalent, so I went more for the feeling of those stories and motifs. So Vikings were DnD but with Operatic overtones. Drama,High Adventure, Death repeat. Elves are battle heavy warriors of the gods. Dwarves are schemers beneath the earth, they can create marvels, but at what price? Monsters target loved ones, and utter your doom as they die. The bad guys are vengeful and devious, and try to wreck anything you hold dear before dying. Magic is dangerous and incredibly scary. Those who mess with it are scarred by the encounter.<br /> Examples:<br /> Woden is a powerful magician who has sacrificed too much for his pantheon, and has been changed by it, Freya is a sorceress of such beauty that prayers to her give you power over others and she herself is rise of many conflicts. Loki was a good sort once but the magic he messed with has changed him more and more, into the creature he is.<br /> <br /> Aztec stories are about being the classic hero, but in a horror story. Knights of the round table meets Lovecraft. Not so much the blood (which is more about conviction and sin) but just what they faced and how. Aztec heroes have to have courage and cleverness in a world that will twist itself trying to kill them. Hordes that try to kill you, mystical pregnancies, part animal part human everything. Death of powerful gods. Flayed gods. And these are the good guys you pray to who are more benevolant than not, but to protect the world, they ask a lot...<br /> Examples:<br /> The Goddess of Filth takes that filth from you and can heal souls, she revels in every putrid thing so you don't have to you are her son, ready to wade into hell and enjoy it.<br /> Quetzalcoatl used his blood to water the world, but he was dead when you were born and every year you lose pieces of yourself that drop as red feathers to stop the process, you must travel to the land of unending dead so you may speak with his undead soul and not get destroyed by his magnitude.<br /> <br /> Chinese stories are fun, awesome and more humourous than not. It is about fun adventures and always about the weird stuff you can get into rather than overcoming them yourself. There are surprising morals behind the hijinks but are much better when missed by the characters until they take it to heart. Anyone can be redeemed and balance is important. Protecting everyday people is higher on the agenda than most of the other pantheons, but that may mean more trouble you can get into. <br /> Examples:<br /> Demons are bad guys, unless they aren't, and some just want to hang out with you, try to kill you, and pronounce you practically related brothers before trying to kill you again.<br /> Sun Wukong just robbed part of the Celestial Bureaucracy and frames you and the Celestial Bureaucracy knows this but at least they can catch you.<br /> You are now the designated driver and caretaker of a very drunk god, good luck.<br /> <br /> Hindu stories, I make as Epic as possible. It is never about killing one monster or saving the princess, you wouldn't be needed if you didn't have to save the world. These are stories where the goodguy gives the bad guy a chance to back down, where honor is more important than life. Where goodness does equate to power, where even the princess after being saved goes through an epic thing herself to prove to the people she is still worthy. Kindness is usually payed in kind, being in love is crossing all boundaries because that is your one true love, and friendship lasts across lifetimes. The gods even have to hold this up or be shamed because they believe it 100%. Also, Bows are the most epic honorable weapon ever.<br /> <br /> At least that was what I tried to do. Also some play off each other, so the campaign is based off of a Hindu threat, but the stuff inbetween is mostly Viking because end of the world works well with them. When you mess up with being an upstanding hero wielding goodness like a sword, the world punished the heroes by putting them into an Aztec story of horror. When the drama runs high, throw in a fun Chinese tale to get everyone relaxed. It is pretty fun and helped my players feel the legends and like they were making new ones without having to learn them. What helped you guys?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5197-kadakithis","name":"kadakithis","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-28T09:05:29-08:00","id":423012,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>kadakithis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/422881-capturing-the-feeling-of-myths#post422881\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> You are now the designated driver and caretaker of a very drunk god, good luck.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>This.<br /> <br /> Awesome.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member